WEBVTT

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
Super freak

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
♪Killer Move

00:00.001 --> 00:00.002
♪Wing Mantis

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
- - ♪Currently writing a fan letter to the
author of his favorite erotic novel series.

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪Miso Udon Whip loaded

00:00.003 --> 00:00.004
♪The Killer Chicken Wings

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪Florsheim Monster

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪Nagoya Strike

00:00.005 --> 00:00.006
♪Usakotsu Laughs Cold-heartedly

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Nails

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Gold

00:00.007 --> 00:00.008
♪Kabukicho First Street

00:00.011 --> 00:01.680
♪-Droopy Ears' Apartment-

00:05.970 --> 00:08.619
Pardon me, General Hengel.

00:08.620 --> 00:10.349
There is something that
I've been meaning to ask you.

00:10.350 --> 00:11.559
What is it?

00:11.560 --> 00:13.899
This isn't an easy question to ask.

00:13.900 --> 00:16.659
But are you, General Hengel,

00:16.660 --> 00:18.309
a lecherous man?

00:18.310 --> 00:19.920
No!

00:20.590 --> 00:22.239
My dear Samiel,

00:22.240 --> 00:26.319
you should really choose
your words more carefully.

00:26.320 --> 00:27.320
Yes, sir.

00:27.700 --> 00:29.459
I am...

00:29.460 --> 00:30.790
a super freak!

00:32.750 --> 00:35.489
General Hengel of Florsheim's
West Tokyo Division.

00:35.490 --> 00:38.590
His IQ is reported to be over 150.

02:14.990 --> 02:16.980
Um, Mr. Red?

02:17.980 --> 02:20.579
I'm glad that you've called us out,

02:20.580 --> 02:23.309
but would you mind us
talking someplace else?

02:23.310 --> 02:24.959
Right here's just fine.

02:24.960 --> 02:26.859
But we're at the peak of summer!

02:26.860 --> 02:29.629
The sunlight's so strong that
my eyes are starting get irritated.

02:29.630 --> 02:30.980
And where exactly are your eyes?!

02:31.880 --> 02:33.639
Oh, can't you tell where they are?

02:33.640 --> 02:36.489
They're actually located
here, on the tip of his antennae.

02:36.490 --> 02:38.329
Nails is actually a snail monster, so-

02:38.330 --> 02:39.539
Who gives a shit?!

02:39.540 --> 02:42.969
Are you guys even going to hear me out?

02:42.970 --> 02:44.239
We will, we will.

02:44.240 --> 02:45.829
Let's pay attention, guys.

02:45.830 --> 02:49.129
It's not everyday that Mr. Red
calls us out for these things.

02:49.130 --> 02:50.860
We'll be extra attentive.

02:51.160 --> 02:52.669
So as I was saying...

02:52.670 --> 02:53.679
What?

02:53.680 --> 02:55.850
Could we please go somewhere else?

02:56.150 --> 03:00.919
You may be okay with the
heat since you're a Sun Fighter,

03:00.920 --> 03:03.319
but I'm sweating balls here.

03:03.320 --> 03:05.119
I said, we're fine here!

03:05.120 --> 03:06.000
Now that you mention it,

03:06.001 --> 03:09.299
I think they were issuing warnings about
photochemical smog in the atmosphere today.

03:09.300 --> 03:10.639
Are you serious?

03:10.640 --> 03:13.449
That's probably why your
eyes feel irritated then.

03:13.450 --> 03:15.499
I really think we should
change venues, Mr. Red.

03:15.500 --> 03:17.439
It's not like you're
going to die or anything.

03:17.440 --> 03:19.039
Why don't we go to a café somewhere?

03:19.040 --> 03:20.040
Those things cost money.

03:20.240 --> 03:23.929
How about Takazu Citizen's
Hall in Mizonokuchi, then?

03:23.930 --> 03:26.780
They don't charge for admission,
plus they've got air conditioning.

03:28.160 --> 03:29.160
Nails!

03:33.210 --> 03:34.809
You know...

03:34.810 --> 03:35.889
Yes?

03:35.890 --> 03:39.740
It doesn't make any sense for an evil monster
to collapse from heat stroke in the first place.

03:40.540 --> 03:42.729
But I've been thinking,

03:42.730 --> 03:44.779
that I've been too easy on you guys lately.

03:44.780 --> 03:45.939
I've been way too nice.

03:45.940 --> 03:48.099
But isn't that a good thing?

03:48.100 --> 03:49.859
I'm sure "niceness" is a quality
essential to every friend of justice-

03:49.860 --> 03:50.790
Are we on the same page here?

03:50.791 --> 03:53.519
Then again, you guys are too laid back too.

03:53.520 --> 03:55.440
Are you guys even trying
to take me out anymore?

03:55.590 --> 03:57.009
Of course we are. Right, guys?

03:57.010 --> 03:59.189
We wanna really fuck you up, Mr. Red!

03:59.190 --> 04:01.520
That's not convincing at all!

04:01.820 --> 04:04.319
I'm so jealous of that punk.

04:04.320 --> 04:05.779
"That punk?"

04:05.780 --> 04:08.169
I'm talking about Shachihokoider Great.

04:08.170 --> 04:10.399
It's me, the really strong guy from Nagoya,

04:10.400 --> 04:13.640
Shachihokoider Great!

04:13.800 --> 04:16.349
Shachihokoider Great?

04:16.350 --> 04:18.269
Oh, I think I read about
him on the Florsheim Times.

04:18.270 --> 04:20.610
He was in our corporate magazine?

04:21.310 --> 04:23.349
Corporate what?

04:23.350 --> 04:29.109
But if I'm not mistaken, Shachihokoider
is originally from Kanagawa, isn't he?

04:29.110 --> 04:29.910
Well, yeah.

04:29.911 --> 04:31.339
He used to be.

04:31.340 --> 04:35.269
He got his character from the Shachihoko
pieces on top of Odawara Castle,

04:35.270 --> 04:38.739
so he moved to Aichi, claiming
that Shachihokos belong in Nagoya.

04:38.740 --> 04:41.679
And since the Shachihoko in
Nagoya are the most famous in Japan,

04:41.680 --> 04:45.439
he became Shachihokoider
Great through that effect.

04:45.440 --> 04:47.119
Although "Great" only signifies the fact

04:47.120 --> 04:51.319
that he replaced the one that used to be
on his head with a bigger, golden version.

04:51.320 --> 04:53.239
Oh, those things come off?

04:53.240 --> 04:54.569
But then again,

04:54.570 --> 04:58.850
I guess you can say he took off because
I'm holding it down here in Kanagawa.

05:01.190 --> 05:04.439
Come again? I don't
think I heard you correctly...

05:04.440 --> 05:05.510
Never mind.

05:05.830 --> 05:09.969
Anyway I ran into him the other day
at the underground malls in Kawasaki.

05:09.970 --> 05:12.079
Let's go eat something.

05:12.080 --> 05:13.329
Okay.

05:13.330 --> 05:15.010
Huh, Mr. Red!

05:15.880 --> 05:18.210
It's been too long!

05:18.810 --> 05:22.269
Apparently he came back to
get his family registry certificate

05:22.270 --> 05:25.150
because he needed it for his
passport to go abroad or something.

05:23.470 --> 05:23.990
Ow!

05:24.170 --> 05:25.150
Sorry.

05:25.151 --> 05:26.219
Who was that?

05:26.220 --> 05:29.309
I could really care less
about why he came back,

05:29.310 --> 05:32.369
but apparently Shachihokoider's
been doing really well.

05:32.370 --> 05:35.139
A Nagoyan Morning Coffee comes
with Toast, Boiled Eggs, Salad,

05:35.140 --> 05:38.190
and Sometimes Some Bananas Punch!

05:38.410 --> 05:40.239
Apparently he's taking his fight
against The Killer Chicken Wings,

05:40.240 --> 05:42.589
Nagoya's evil organization,
to the next level.

05:42.590 --> 05:45.190
And boy was he trying to
show it off in front of Kayoko.

05:45.990 --> 05:49.229
Did you guys ever hear about how I
stopped the explosion at Nagoya Castle?

05:49.230 --> 05:50.859
I never really liked
that guy to begin with.

05:50.860 --> 05:52.079
He's really insensitive.

05:52.080 --> 05:54.569
Plus he talks ever so politely to
me even though we're the same age,

05:54.570 --> 05:57.210
and all he ever does is talk about himself.

05:57.710 --> 05:59.759
But then again,

05:59.760 --> 06:01.769
he's apparently busy everyday.

06:01.770 --> 06:04.619
He says he keeps getting into
these life or death fights with monsters,

06:04.620 --> 06:06.730
which makes everyone so
thankful that heroes exist.

06:08.630 --> 06:11.419
Is <i>that</i> what got you so worked up today?

06:11.420 --> 06:13.459
Yeah, what's so funny about it?

06:13.460 --> 06:15.839
He's been feeding you lies.

06:15.840 --> 06:19.870
I was actually talking to my nephew over at
the Killer Chicken Wings not too long ago,

06:20.190 --> 06:25.089
and there was not even a single mention
of Shachihokoider in that conversation.

06:25.090 --> 06:27.229
I don't think they even know he exists.

06:27.230 --> 06:28.220
For real?

06:28.220 --> 06:29.150
Yeah.

06:29.151 --> 06:31.179
Don't you think it's weird for
someone to suddenly go abroad,

06:31.180 --> 06:33.420
if he's really trying to take
a fight to the next level?

06:34.760 --> 06:37.929
I've always had my suspicions
since he's pretty weak.

06:37.930 --> 06:40.419
It was really nothing
to get worked up about.

06:40.420 --> 06:42.709
I guess you were worried
for nothing, Mr. Red.

06:42.710 --> 06:44.000
So that's how it is.

06:44.400 --> 06:47.859
That damn punk...

06:47.860 --> 06:49.799
So, Mr. Red?

06:49.800 --> 06:52.250
Is there anything else
you'd like to talk about?

06:53.400 --> 06:55.010
Is there anything...

06:55.650 --> 06:56.650
you'd like to talk about?

06:57.650 --> 06:58.740
Anything?

07:00.450 --> 07:03.189
Not really.

07:03.190 --> 07:06.079
Then, may we be excused?

07:06.080 --> 07:07.510
Oh. Yeah.

07:09.910 --> 07:11.879
Are you feeling better now, Nails?

07:11.880 --> 07:14.199
Yes, much better after the nap.

07:14.200 --> 07:17.449
I guess there are different
types of heroes in the world.

07:17.450 --> 07:20.479
Yeah. I don't like the
ones that lie, though.

07:20.480 --> 07:23.206
You'd think it'd go against everything
that a friend of justice stands for.

07:23.230 --> 07:24.669
Right?

07:24.670 --> 07:27.459
We're so lucky to have
Mr. Red as our enemy.

07:27.460 --> 07:29.329
He's a little tough on us, though.

07:29.330 --> 07:30.799
Just "a little?"

07:30.800 --> 07:34.419
But he's doing that to make us better.

07:34.420 --> 07:36.549
He wouldn't get all
angry like that if he wasn't.

07:36.550 --> 07:38.289
Especially since we're after his life.

07:38.290 --> 07:39.809
You've got a point there.

07:39.810 --> 07:41.740
Yup.

07:45.870 --> 07:47.239
What's wrong?

07:47.240 --> 07:50.269
Something still doesn't add up.

07:50.270 --> 07:51.729
Astro Fighter Sunred.

07:51.730 --> 07:53.929
This is a story of the
conflict between good and evil

07:53.930 --> 07:56.830
that takes place in the city of Kawasaki.

08:02.170 --> 08:04.629
What can I do?

08:04.630 --> 08:09.019
Florsheim's sworn mortal
enemy, Astro Fighter Sunred.

08:09.020 --> 08:12.290
How can I take him down?

08:13.840 --> 08:16.169
Come on, do I have to do this?

08:16.170 --> 08:17.819
Stop complaining.

08:17.820 --> 08:20.639
There are eggs in that bag
so don't let it shake, okay?

08:20.640 --> 08:21.669
I know.

08:21.670 --> 08:22.630
You naggy little...

08:22.631 --> 08:23.639
What?

08:23.640 --> 08:25.080
Nothing at all.

08:26.550 --> 08:27.620
I got it!

08:30.710 --> 08:33.470
Guest coming through!

08:33.610 --> 08:35.160
Oh, Usakotsu.

08:35.760 --> 08:37.069
Long time no see.

08:37.070 --> 08:40.039
Droopy Ears! It's really been too long.

08:40.040 --> 08:42.070
Don't call me that here.

08:42.470 --> 08:44.850
My name here is...

08:45.530 --> 08:46.579
Reiji.

08:46.580 --> 08:48.009
Oh my god, he's too cute!

08:48.010 --> 08:50.149
Is this a friend of yours, Reiji?

08:50.150 --> 08:52.069
He's an underclassman
from my high school days.

08:52.070 --> 08:55.259
You're too cute, Reiji.

08:55.260 --> 08:56.929
Hey, manager.

08:56.930 --> 08:58.649
Don't forget about me!

08:58.650 --> 09:01.750
I haven't. I'll show you to our table.

09:02.140 --> 09:04.709
Here's a toast to our long-delayed reunion.

09:04.710 --> 09:06.750
Cheers!

09:07.130 --> 09:10.259
You should really be acquainted
with the taste of alcohol by this age.

09:10.260 --> 09:11.349
I'm sorry.

09:11.350 --> 09:14.569
I just get really sleepy
real fast when I drink.

09:14.570 --> 09:17.449
You can say you truly start
appreciating the taste of alcohol

09:17.450 --> 09:19.440
when life really starts going downhill.

09:20.440 --> 09:24.919
Well, I see you're still as
popular as ever, Droopy Ears.

09:24.920 --> 09:27.119
It's my job to be popular.

09:27.120 --> 09:29.549
I've got so much respect for you right now.

09:29.550 --> 09:31.609
So what did you want to talk about?

09:31.610 --> 09:32.470
Is it about money?

09:32.471 --> 09:34.629
Oh, yeah. I mean, no!

09:34.630 --> 09:35.580
Hear me out on this one.

09:35.581 --> 09:38.390
There's this guy that our
organization's been at war with.

09:38.890 --> 09:40.030
At war?

09:41.270 --> 09:42.749
I see.

09:42.750 --> 09:45.769
So there's a girl who's been
taking care of this Red guy, you say?

09:45.770 --> 09:48.309
Yes, I'm pretty sure Red's
going to implode without a word

09:48.310 --> 09:51.569
if Kayoko were to dump him.

09:51.570 --> 09:53.789
So basically what you're saying,

09:53.790 --> 09:57.679
is that you want me, the
number one host in Kabukicho,

09:57.680 --> 10:00.149
to go break those two up?

10:00.150 --> 10:01.559
Exactly.

10:01.560 --> 10:04.369
Why not. I'm used to having
others spite me out of jealousy.

10:04.370 --> 10:06.019
So you'll really do it?

10:06.020 --> 10:08.579
World domination isn't my thing,

10:08.580 --> 10:10.399
but I'll do it for my cute Usa.

10:10.400 --> 10:11.929
Thank you so much!

10:11.930 --> 10:15.640
I guess duty calls.

10:15.820 --> 10:18.429
Here, use this for your cab ride home.

10:18.430 --> 10:19.889
We're not in any kind of
economic recession though.

10:19.890 --> 10:22.359
It's okay, just take it.

10:22.360 --> 10:24.400
Take care of yourself now. Bye.

10:25.100 --> 10:27.710
He's so cool.

10:29.080 --> 10:31.619
She should pass by if we wait here.

10:31.620 --> 10:33.919
I don't usually work mornings.

10:33.920 --> 10:35.189
I'm so sorry.

10:35.190 --> 10:36.590
Don't worry about it.

10:37.950 --> 10:38.730
Is that her?

10:38.731 --> 10:40.030
Yeah.

10:40.930 --> 10:42.969
Looks like half the
job's been done already.

10:42.970 --> 10:44.030
Good luck!

10:56.320 --> 10:58.010
What's this?

10:59.650 --> 11:00.860
Cheers!

11:01.660 --> 11:04.139
I wonder if Red's seen the photo already.

11:04.140 --> 11:07.079
Once he sees how much she wants me,

11:07.080 --> 11:11.939
he will most likely admit that he's lost,

11:11.940 --> 11:14.910
and break things off with the girl himself.

11:18.350 --> 11:19.869
Hey guess what?

11:19.870 --> 11:24.010
I saw this really cute dog this morning.

11:26.860 --> 11:30.000
I'm used to having others
spite me out of jealousy.
